			"type": "text",
			"text": "Moradisaurus is a captorhinid from the Late Permian Moradi Formation of Niger. At 2 meters in length, it is the largest member of its family. It inhabited an equatorial locality home to a unique fauna consisting mostly of pareiasaurs and temnospondyls, with considerably fewer therapsids than other contemporary formations. Like other captorhinids, Moradisaurus had multiple rows of grinding teeth, suggesting a herbivorous lifestyle."
